    "event": "step_completed",
    "step": {
      "input_id": "step-1",
      "payload": "I'm auditing a Python project before a release. Set it up by running this exact command in the workspace:\n\n```bash\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport os, random\nrandom.seed(4592)\nverbs = [\"handle\", \"validate\", \"cache\", \"log\", \"retry\", \"normalize\", \"document\", \"test\"]\nnouns = [\"empty input\", \"unicode names\", \"timeouts\", \"negative totals\", \"missing config\", \"large files\", \"duplicate ids\", \"stale tokens\"]\nmods = [\"orders\", \"users\", \"billing\", \"report\", \"auth\", \"storage\", \"notify\", \"search\", \"export\", \"cli\"]\npaths = [\"app/%s.py\" % m for m in mods] + [\"app/build/%s.py\" % m for m in (\"pipeline\", \"package\", \"release\", \"assets\")]\nfor path in paths:\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n    name = os.path.splitext(os.path.basename(path))[0]\n    lines = []\n    for i in range(random.randint(2, 4)):\n        lines += [\"def %s_step_%d(data):\" % (name, i)]\n        if random.random() < 0.35:\n            lines += [\"    # TODO: %s %s\" % (random.choice(verbs), random.choice(nouns))]\n        lines += [\"    return data\", \"\"]\n    with open(path, \"w\") as f:\n        f.write(\"\\n\".join(lines))\nfor d in (\"app\", \"app/build\"):\n    open(os.path.join(d, \"__init__.py\"), \"w\").close()\nPY\n```\n\nThen tell me how many TODO comments the project contains in total, and list each one with its file path and line number. Don't change any files.",
      "invocation": {
        "output": "I'll run the setup command as given, then search the generated files for TODO comments without modifying anything.Setup completed with exit code 0. Now I'll search the tree for TODO comments.The glob pattern only surfaced top-level modules, so I'll verify the `app/build` package exists and search it separately before concluding the count.Ran the setup command exactly as given (exit code 0), then searched without modifying anything.\n\nTotal: **20 TODO comments**.\n\n| File | Line | Comment |\n|---|---|---|\n| app/auth.py | 5 | `# TODO: retry duplicate ids` |\n| app/billing.py | 8 | `# TODO: test missing config` |\n| app/build/assets.py | 5 | `# TODO: document timeouts` |\n| app/build/pipeline.py | 5 | `# TODO: handle timeouts` |\n| app/build/pipeline.py | 9 | `# TODO: retry stale tokens` |\n| app/cli.py | 2 | `# TODO: test large files` |\n| app/cli.py | 9 | `# TODO: validate stale tokens` |\n| app/export.py | 5 | `# TODO: retry unicode names` |\n| app/notify.py | 8 | `# TODO: normalize stale tokens` |\n| app/orders.py | 2 | `# TODO: handle negative totals` |\n| app/orders.py | 6 | `# TODO: validate duplicate ids` |\n| app/report.py | 5 | `# TODO: document empty input` |\n| app/report.py | 9 | `# TODO: document timeouts` |\n| app/report.py | 13 | `# TODO: validate timeouts` |\n| app/storage.py | 2 | `# TODO: cache duplicate ids` |\n| app/storage.py | 6 | `# TODO: log empty input` |\n| app/storage.py | 13 | `# TODO: normalize duplicate ids` |\n| app/users.py | 5 | `# TODO: cache negative totals` |\n| app/users.py | 9 | `# TODO: test duplicate ids` |\n| app/users.py | 13 | `# TODO: cache large files` |\n\nPer-file counts: `users.py`, `report.py`, `storage.py` 3 each; `orders.py`, `cli.py`, `pipeline.py` 2 each; `auth.py`, `billing.py`, `assets.py`, `export.py`, `notify.py` 1 each. Files with none: `app/search.py`, `app/build/package.py`, `app/build/release.py`, and both `__init__.py` files.\n\nOne audit note: my first pass with the search tool reported only 17 matches because it did not descend into `app/build/`, and a `app/**/*.py` glob listed only the top-level modules. I re-verified with a recursive shell search (`grep -rn 'TODO' app`), which found the 3 additional hits in `app/build/` — 20 is the correct total, so don't rely on that glob pattern alone for this tree.",
